modation having lost  their homes what would you like to see  done to help these people yeah there's a  thing called the hidden homelessness  which is is not necessarily the people  excuse me you see on the street but  young people who have had to leave their  home for various reasons may be getting  into fights and arguments with their  family over things and you know they  they might end up on buses through the  night or trains back and forth or sort  of couchsurfing their friends houses and  I think what I'd love to see is is first  of all more support especially with  things like mental health which is kind  of on the rise and and thankfully more  and more people are talking but I think  still more needs to be done and secondly  on a long-term basis there needs to be  more affordable housing and better  checks on on people who rent houses  because I think I think it's got to a  point where people are being sort of  forcibly removed from rented housing you  know with with very short notice and  that's actually one of the big reasons  why people end up on the on the street  very quickly yeah of course and I think  at this time of year as well with the  weather the winter it really does bring  it to the fore a kind gesture can go a  long way can't it what would be your  message to people if they want to do  something to help  I yeah I think that honestly the  interaction is such an important thing  if you see somebody on the street that's  cold you know if you felt any anything  you can offer them whether it you know  be an umbrella or a blanket or a coat  but also you know just that exchange and  and and taking the time to stop and talk  to someone ask their name you know  sometimes they might not want to talk  but if they do want to talk you know do  do that obviously you know change and  food does help too but I honestly think  just taking the time and showing that  you've noticed them so many people get  ignored and and you know often them I've  seen videos lately which is which is an  absolute disgrace where people can get  on late nights out on people are drunk  and walking past homeless people they  can get abused and taunted and I think  that's an absolute disgrace and I think  that we just have to be more conscious  of that person being another human being  like yourself and you know and I just  want more people to to help each other  and be more compassionate and it and if  I can sort of try and you know teach my  fans that and younger people that then I  think it could be a nicer place  absolutely and it's not just about  offering homeless people a safe  environment it's about offering them a  way of climbing out of that situation  isn't it yeah once you once you become  homeless you can lose everything very  quickly you can lose your family your  friends you know your your the social  sort of network and you know you can  lose your confidence and it's it's a  it's a really really terrifying thing to  find yourself that lonely and without  anyone around you and so you know crisis  is so good  helping people at this time of year you  know short term people coming in and  we've got blankets and showers and food  and you know tea and and so there's that  but yeah god I kind of have so I had a  complete blank because I've got  distracted but don't worry  yeah I know sorry it's because I was  looking into the canteen and got  completely distracted oops I'm sorry  what was the question  just what more can people do I mean  obviously you you are doing some great  work with crisis and raising awareness  here if people want to also help what  can they do do you need more donations  for instance yep don't donations help  volunteering you can apply to volunteer  maybe not for this year but definitely  for next year and I think just just  being conscious and just knowing that  it's a problem knowing that it's a  problem on the rise and and you know and  and spreading that awareness and talking  about it and I think sometimes you know  it's something that a problem that  people kind of have to ignore because  it's it's so you know it's so horrible  to see as they're sad to see but really  it does need  come from the top from the government  and there needs to be more of a  political force
 

